        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Loughborough Students' Union, Loughborough University, Loughborough College, RNIB College Loughborough\n- Places: Loughborough, Leicestershire, East Midlands, England\n- Concepts: public research university, students' union\n\nFacts:\n- In 1909, the institution that became Loughborough University began as the Loughborough Technical Institute with a focus on skills and knowledge directly applicable in the wider world.\n- In 1966, Loughborough University became a university.\n- Loughborough University is a public research university located in the market town of Loughborough, Leicestershire, in the East Midlands of England.\n- Loughborough University uses the abbreviation Lough for post-nominals.\n- Loughborough Students' Union, also known as LSU, is the students' union for members from Loughborough University, Loughborough College, and RNIB College Loughborough.",
